          <change when="2021-08-20T07:39:54-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Submit - Entered corrections from BL XII 228, excerpted from Gascou, CE 77 (2002) 332. The symbol interpreted as (ἀρτάβαι) in lins1ff. does not have the right shape for it (Gascou, ibid.); I leave it as it is for now. In the anachronistic (πυροῦ ἀρτάβαι) in lins11–12 (Gascou, ibid.; Clarysse, BASP 51 (2014) 105 n. 17), (πυροῦ) in lins11–12 (and 14–15) is shown in the apparatus as a cross, but this is part of the earlier writing, re-read by Gascou. I have moved (πυροῦ) to the deprecated reading, although it is not acknowledged as such in the print sources.</change>
